            <ArticleTitle>Alteration of catecholamine concentration in urine and ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Concentration of catecholamines (Adrenaline and Noradrenaline) was determined in the urine collected for 24 h from normal subjects and those with painful ischemic cardiopathy. Statistically significant results were obtained only for adrenaline whose concentration increased in the above mentioned pathological state.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
